From: ann-harness-amd CAGRA follow-on
Subject: [PATCH] ut: default GPU CAGRA build_algo to NN_DESCENT

On consumer gfx1100, hipVS CAGRA with default IVF_PQ intermediate graph
build yields recall 0.0 (or throws in Python). Library smoke with
build_algo=nn_descent reaches recall 1.0. Knowhere Catch2 cagra_gen()
omitted BUILD_ALGO (IVF_PQ default); Hamming tests already set ITERATIVE
and pass. Set NN_DESCENT for the shared cagra_gen used by L2/bitset/TopK/
serialize paths.

---
 tests/ut/test_gpu_search.cc | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/tests/ut/test_gpu_search.cc b/tests/ut/test_gpu_search.cc
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/tests/ut/test_gpu_search.cc
+++ b/tests/ut/test_gpu_search.cc
@@ -61,6 +61,7 @@ TEST_CASE("Test All GPU Index", "[search]") {
     auto cagra_gen = [base_gen]() {
         knowhere::Json json = base_gen();
         json[knowhere::indexparam::INTERMEDIATE_GRAPH_DEGREE] = 64;
         json[knowhere::indexparam::GRAPH_DEGREE] = 32;
         json[knowhere::indexparam::ITOPK_SIZE] = 128;
+        json[knowhere::indexparam::BUILD_ALGO] = "NN_DESCENT";
         return json;
     };
 
-- 
